    {
      "source": "<tbody><tr>\n<td class=\"icon\">\n<i class=\"fa icon-note\" title=\"Note\"></i>\n</td>\n<td class=\"content\">\nIt is definitely reasonable to mark read-only queries as such by setting the <code>readOnly</code> flag.\nThis does not, however, act as a check that you do not trigger a manipulating query (although some databases reject <code>INSERT</code> and <code>UPDATE</code> statements inside a read-only transaction).\nInstead, the <code>readOnly</code> flag is propagated as a hint to the underlying JDBC driver for performance optimizations.\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>",
      "translation": "<td class=\"icon\">\n<i class=\"fa icon-note\" title=\"Note\"></i>\n</td>\n<td class=\"content\">\n将只读查询标记为只读（通过设置 <code>readOnly</code> 标志）无疑是合理的。然而，这并不能防止您触发修改性查询（尽管某些数据库会拒绝在只读事务中执行 <code>INSERT</code> 和 <code>UPDATE</code> 语句）。实际上，<code>readOnly</code> 标志是作为提示传递给底层 JDBC 驱动程序的，以便进行性能优化。\n</td>\n</tr>",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "<tbody><tr>\n<td class=\"icon\">\n<i class=\"fa icon-note\" title=\"Note\"></i>\n</td>\n<td class=\"content\">\n<code>@Lock</code> is currently not supported on string-based queries.\nQuery-methods created with <code>@Query</code> will ignore the locking information provided by the <code>@Lock</code>,\nUsing <code>@Lock</code> on string-based queries will result in a warning in logs.\nFuture versions will throw an exception.\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>",
      "translation": "<tbody><tr>\n<td class=\"icon\">\n<i class=\"fa icon-note\" title=\"Note\"></i>\n</td>\n<td class=\"content\">\n<code>@Lock</code> 目前不支持用于基于字符串的查询。\n使用 <code>@Query</code> 创建的查询方法将忽略 <code>@Lock</code> 提供的锁信息，\n在基于字符串的查询上使用 <code>@Lock</code> 将在日志中产生警告。\n未来版本将抛出异常。\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "<button class=\"nav-item-toggle\"></button>\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"../index.html\">Overview</a>\n<ul class=\"nav-list\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\" data-depth=\"2\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"../commons/upgrade.html\">Upgrading Spring Data</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>",
      "translation": "<button class=\"nav-item-toggle\"></button>\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"../index.html\">概览</a>\n<ul class=\"nav-list\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\" data-depth=\"2\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"../commons/upgrade.html\">升级 Spring Data</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "<tbody><tr>\n<td class=\"icon\">\n<i class=\"fa icon-note\" title=\"Note\"></i>\n</td>\n<td class=\"content\">\nIt is highly recommended to make query methods transactional.\nThese methods might execute more than one query in order to populate an entity.\nWithout a common transaction Spring Data JDBC executes the queries in different connections.\nThis may put excessive strain on the connection pool and might even lead to deadlocks when multiple methods request a fresh connection while holding on to one.\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>",
      "translation": "<tr>\n<td class=\"icon\">\n<i class=\"fa icon-note\" title=\"Note\"></i>\n</td>\n<td class=\"content\">\n强烈建议将查询方法设置为事务性。\n这些方法可能需要执行多个查询以填充实体对象。\n如果没有统一的事务，Spring Data JDBC 将在不同的连接中执行这些查询。\n这可能会对连接池造成过大压力，甚至可能导致死锁，特别是在多个方法在持有某个连接的同时请求新连接的情况下。\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>",
      "count": 1
    },
